pt":"When I heard Red Gravy was moving Uptown and serving dinner, I knew I had to get over there! I was excited to visit Red Gravy on a recent date night with my fiance David. The quaint atmosphere transports you and the smell of delicious food is intoxicating. We started with the Nanni -- miniature meatballs served with red gravy and fresh ricotta. These meatballs were anything but mini, and the red gravy and ricotta balanced the flavors of the meatballs well. For an entree, we got Red Gravy's famous lasagna Bolognese, which is layers of ricotta, mozzarella and Bolognese layered delicately together and served fresh-baked from the oven. The lasagna is made fresh, so there's a 30-minute wait ti..."},{"business_id":"ofXLzGLYFVb4AFFmNV837g","review_id":"5NlJV6dKHthZLc9IIPWU2A","date":"2021-04-04T18:49:34","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8925530314445496,"text_excerpt":"We made our 1st time visit for Easter Brunch, and we're still celebrating the choice we made. (You know I studied Easter brunch menus for weeks, lol) Everything about our experience was right, from the service to the cocktails to the food. I was sent the wrong cocktail-which I didn't even notice- and a few minutes later was brought the correct one. The Easter bread that we began with was delicious and a tradition that I hope to continue. Melissa ordered the Tuscan shrimp and grits, which she proclaimed to be better than her perennial favorite crawfish ettoufee. My Peter Rabbit entrée was fried green tomatoes covered with rabbit sausage, scrambled eggs, and hollandaise sauce. I didn't leav..."},{"business_id":"ofXLzGLYFVb4AFFmNV837g","review_id":"ZmS9Z7fdHIjxZrDEMTpFww","date":"2021-11-06T23:54:58","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8880276679992676,"text_excerpt":"What a great restaurant! The staff, Mark in particular, was astounding. I had sausage and ricotta homemade ravioli with Pomodoro sauce! Do yourself a favor and enjoy this restaurant!"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
